 "note": {
  "h": "一 · Il · the plain",
  "p": "Pyongwon is the wide plain: open ground that feeds every living thing and stretches as far as you can see. The floor line is one straight line, 一, walked back and forth. The plan shows it as three passes along that one line: out and toward da, then back toward ra, then toward da again."
 },
 "footer": "Move numbers follow the 14 steps of the NBTKDA chart; techniques in the same step share a number (3-1 kick, 3-2 kick, 3-3 and 3-4 blocks). Kukkiwon counts 21 movements. Finish with <b>Baro</b>: bring the left foot back beside the right into closed stance, hands overlapped, at the starting point.",
